        0.8282404847743057
      ]
    },
    {
      "shape_id": 7,
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "To make psychology scientifically rigorous, researchers turned to animal models. They focused on the simplest behaviors—responses to stimuli—that could be quantified, moving away from abstract concepts to measurable cause-and-effect relationships.",
      "alt_text": "Text 4",
      "manim_bbox": [
